{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1109872-investigating-the-abyss","id":1109872,"title":"Investigating the Abyss","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-30T12:48:01-07:00","id":1109872,"title":"Investigating the Abyss","content":"Hello, everyone!<br /> <br /> I am afraid I missed it on the main book, but I have some questions about the Abyss. Although Prime is the Arcana of Truth, when I first read Mage 2nd Edition I was under the impression that it could also detect the absence of Truth (the Abyss). In this sense, I allowed my players to detect threads of the Abyss with Prime Sight, etc.<br /> <br /> Upon a second reading of Mage 2nd Edition, I started to wonder if that was right at all. There is nothing on Prime Sight that says it can detect the Abyss, and if the Abyss is the absence of magic, then maybe the Awakened's worst enemy is also the only thing they actually blind to? I started to really dig the idea that the Abyss must be investigated without the support of the usual 'I use spell, I know the plot' spells and mechanics of Mage, and players must rely on their guile and mundane skills to do it.<br /> <br /> Is there ANY truth to this reasoning? What is the relationship between the Abyss and the Sights? What is your take on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T13:04:22-07:00","id":1109887,"title":"","content":"The Abyss is not Lies. It is Untrue.<br /> <br /> As in, it is a far, far more complex thing than simple deception-it's that, but also misinterpretation, ignorance, confusion, incomplete information, the gap between what is said and what is understood too. A deliberate lie implies the presence of truth, but that which is untrue has no such limitations of being needed to compared to petty things like fact.<br /> <br /> In a less spiritual sense, you're precisely right-the Awakened aren't precisely blind to the Void, but spoilers from Sanctum and Sigil have revealed that the Abyss being the source of a phenomenon makes it just as hard to mystically grok as things completely unrelated to the Supernal but are still supernatural. A gulmoth is not just anti-magic, it's a glitch in reality that has been given will of its own and a desire to undo normal functions of reality. And the thing about glitches is that they arise from an otherwise functional system, and until it's really closely inspected, you can't actually see the glitch.<br /> <br /> The Annunaki? Well, they're incarnations of what would happen if the glitches <i>were</i> the normal system","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T13:31:42-07:00","id":1109904,"title":"","content":"In my games, I treat Mage Sight of all types as not being useful for understanding Abyssal stuff, unless you've got some kind of weird power like the Abyss Sight from Grimoire of Grimoires, or a Legacy Attainment. As you said, it makes things exciting when the PCs' go-to tool doesn't work and they need to use other avenues.<br /> <br /> I do let them gain information on specific phenomena by using spellcasting. Like &quot;Know Spirit&quot; mostly works on manifested Gulmoth, (although it might make you Resonant), and the basic traits of an Abyssal computer virus or Environmental Tilt could be understood using Forces. But you can't get the kind of deep understanding that comes with Scrutiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}